<!--Post: 1077--><!--Time: 1096638739-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1077"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 01, 2004 - 6:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it my imagination, or does the young version resemble the Green River Killer and the aged version looks like Robert Durst? I think that he tuned in murderers, but got the wrong signal.  And I do believe that the right psychic can solve a case, so I am not a skeptic.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1077-->
<!--Post: 1079--><!--Time: 1096666500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1079"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, October 01, 2004 - 2:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Teardrop. <BR>I wonder why they don&#39;t make the sketches public? Or any composite police sketches?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1079-->
<!--Post: 1083--><!--Time: 1096747215-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1083"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blgneme<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blgneme<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, October 02, 2004 - 1:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->teardrop , <BR> <BR>have you seen these sketches? <BR>where are they available?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1083-->
<!--Post: 1085--><!--Time: 1096747630-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1085"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, October 02, 2004 - 1:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here they are:  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/images/btk1.jpg" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/images/btk1.jpg</a>  <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/images/btk2.jpg" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/images/btk2.jpg</a>  <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/images/btk3.jpg" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/images/btk3.jpg</a> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1085-->
<!--Post: 1103--><!--Time: 1096977060-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1103"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bookworm<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bookworm<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, October 05, 2004 - 4:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you Tom. <BR> <BR>I wonder if they were made about the same time or not, because of the third sketch being older. <BR> <BR>To me the first and second do look similar except for the hair, and the third one looks like an older version of the first sketch.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1103-->
<!--Post: 1111--><!--Time: 1097113441-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1111"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Blgneme<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Blgneme<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, October 06, 2004 - 6:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->10 HOURS <BR>600 MILES.... <BR>A DIRECT STRAIGHT LINE.... <BR> <BR>map it out.... <BR> <BR>doesnt popular recent theory suggest that the bum is not living in kansas anymore??? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1111-->
<!--Post: 2868--><!--Time: 1104211639-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2868"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Seesthru<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Seesthru<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->9-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 9:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nondescript, that&#39;s BTK. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2868-->
<!--Post: 4108--><!--Time: 1105678161-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4108"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 8:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bookworm, when the news story about the three sketches was shown on local TV, KAKE said that the psychic Dennis McKenzie described what he felt from visiting the crime scenes and an artist rendered the sketches. The sketches were in a large envelope and the psychic took them out and presented them to WPD, so they were probably drawn at the same time. However, the two that are similar seem to be drawn by the same sketch artist, but the style of the second one, with long hair, looks totally different. If I would venture to guess, it may be that the sketch artist only had time for two sketches and the psychic or another person drew the one with long hair.  <BR> <BR>Blgneme: Are you still here? By 600 miles from Wichita, do you mean San Antonio? Just curious. <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4108-->
<!--Post: 4186--><!--Time: 1105846005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4186"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bluepete<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bluepete<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 7:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Fly, <BR> <BR>for your satisfaction...not S.A. but Houston.. <BR> <BR>since July poster has opinions daily except in days preceding and just after btk drops ... <BR> <BR>and currently nothing from poster in several days so look for activity.. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4186-->
<!--Post: 6084--><!--Time: 1107530768-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6084"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Km<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Km<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 7:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A few days before the psychic&#39;s sketch of what BTK might look like now, a man asked me if I wanted a ride even though I was walking through a parking lot.  When I opened the paper on the morning that the sketch appeared, I really got the creeps.  It looked just like the same man who wanted to give me a ride!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
